%description:

Tcp.fastopenServerEnabled:off -- host2 gives no cookie.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "TCP Fast Open (RFC 7413), server: give cookies, and deliver the data of a
SYN with a valid cookie to the application before the handshake completes".

The classes: off (false, the default), on (true), and changed (the value changes during the
run; the parameter is @mutable). The code: TcpConnection::processFastOpenCookieBytes() gives a
cookie at a request and checks a cookie, and TcpConnection::processSynInListen()
delivers the data of a SYN with a valid cookie; without Fast Open, the server ignores the
cookie options (RFC 7413 section 4.2). This test separates "off" from "on".

Host under test: host2, the server; host1 is a Fast Open client (precondition). host1 opens connection 1 at 0.1 s with Fast Open, which requests a cookie; at 0.5 s it opens
connection 2 with Fast Open and sends 500 bytes, which go on the SYN when host1 has a cookie
of host2. Observation: level 1, the SYN-ACK of connection 1 carries no Fast Open option; the SYN of
connection 2 requests a cookie again, and its SYN-ACK acknowledges only the SYN.

%# parameter: Tcp.fastopenServerEnabled
%# class: off
%# value: false
%# key: *.host2.tcp.fastopenServerEnabled
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "TcpMutations.h"
#include "TcpTestApp.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpFastopenServerEnabledOff")
        .act(action().at(0.1).run<TcpTestApp>("host1.app[0]", [](TcpTestApp& app) { app.socket().connect(app.addressOf("host2"), 1000, true); })
                 .describe("host1 opens connection 1 with Fast Open"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
                  .first()
                  .assertEvent([](const MatchContext& context) {
                      std::string cookie = tcpFastOpenCookieOf(context.event.packet);
                      return cookie == "";
                  })
                  .describe("the SYN of connection 1: a cookie request")
                  .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == true")
                  .first()
                  .assertEvent([](const MatchContext& context) {
                      std::string cookie = tcpFastOpenCookieOf(context.event.packet);
                      return cookie == "-";
                  })
                  .describe("the SYN-ACK of connection 1: no cookie")
                  .within(0.5))
        .act(action().at(0.5).run<TcpTestApp>("host1.app[1]", [](TcpTestApp& app) { app.socket().connect(app.addressOf("host2"), 1000, true); app.sendData(app.socket(), 500); })
                 .describe("host1 opens connection 2 with Fast Open, and sends 500 bytes"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
                  .capture("isn2", "tcp.sequenceNo")
                  .first()
                  .assertEvent([](const MatchContext& context) {
                      std::string cookie = tcpFastOpenCookieOf(context.event.packet);
                      return cookie == "";
                  })
                  .describe("the SYN of connection 2: a cookie request again")
                  .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == true")
             .first()
                  .assertPacket("tcp.ackNo == {isn2} + 1")
             .describe("the SYN-ACK of connection 2 acknowledges only the SYN")
             .within(0.5));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpFastopenServerEnabledOff compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host2.tcp.fastopenServerEnabled = false    # the parameter under test
*.host1.tcp.fastopenClientEnabled = true
*.host1.numApps = 2
*.host1.app[*].typename = "TcpTestApp"
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpFastopenServerEnabledOff: PASS
